  "note": "Total Assets = Total Liabilities + Equity reconciles exactly. Interest income minus interest paid = net interest income exactly; PBT (-133,474,097) minus tax (-243,780,544) = net profit 110,306,447 exactly — the large negative tax figure is a deferred-tax benefit, not an error. The bank's own 2018 Q1 report restates this quarter's EPS comparative to 0.15 (vs 0.16 contemporaneous here) — a bonus-share weighted-average-share restatement (paid-up capital rose from 6,738,936,140 at this date to 7,581,303,150 by Mar-2018). Contemporaneous value (0.16) is kept per project convention."
